1
00:00:00,660 --> 00:00:05,100
At 12:05 today, Michael Jackson
was taken into custody.

2
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:07,600
And so it began -

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:11,300
the most divisive
and controversial trial in history.

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:13,500
Pervert, pervert, pervert!

5
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:16,740
In the dock, a global megastar.

6
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:20,940
The most famous entertainer
the world had ever known.

7
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:22,140
His accusers,

8
00:00:22,340 --> 00:00:26,000
young men who claim to have seen
a very private side to him.

9
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:29,860
Michael Jackson was allegedly
sleeping in bed with little boys.

10
00:00:30,060 --> 00:00:34,200
It turned into a courtroom drama
like no other...

11
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:38,540
He had to go after these two boys
with some ferocity.

12
00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:40,380
..full of star witnesses...

13
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:43,900
Jay Leno came in,
Macaulay Culkin, of course.

14
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:47,420
We were expecting
Diana Ross and Liz Taylor.

15
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:49,320
..shocking revelations...

16
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:51,220
He put his hand in my pants.

17
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:52,140
..plot twists...

18
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:53,660
When she actually gave evidence,

19
00:00:53,860 --> 00:00:56,460
she did the reverse
and supported the defence.

20
00:00:56,660 --> 00:00:58,260
She really did kind of this 180.

21
00:00:58,460 --> 00:00:59,780
..and disappearing acts.

22
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:03,500
We all settle into court,
and then there's no Michael Jackson.

23
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:06,300
With access to people
who were really there...

24
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:10,420
I remember thinking, "Here he comes,
and he's wearing pyjamas."

25
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:12,940
..who witnessed
every dramatic twist and turn...

26
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:15,100
Judge Melville was very upset.

27
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:18,140
Do you want me to shut
this trial down this afternoon?

28
00:01:18,340 --> 00:01:20,340
..this is the whole truth...

29
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:23,740
He looked terrified,
just like he was scared to death.

30
00:01:23,940 --> 00:01:26,100
..of a trial
that shocked the world...

31
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:29,980
That seems to be game, set, match.
Trial's over. You're guilty.

32
00:01:30,180 --> 00:01:32,260
..and changed many lives forever.

33
00:01:32,460 --> 00:01:38,740
It was an absolutely extraordinary
moment in criminal history.

34
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:47,060
November 2003.

35
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:51,980
The world's most famous man,
singer Michael Jackson, is arrested

36
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:56,900
and charged with sexually abusing
a 13-year-old boy, Gavin Arvizo,

37
00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:59,500
at his home, the Neverland Ranch.

38
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:03,680
Michael Jackson has now surrendered
into police custody behind me,

39
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:07,860
a crushing humiliation for one
of the world's great entertainers,

40
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:12,180
right now being read those charges
of child molestation.

41
00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:14,740
The prosecution's intent

42
00:02:14,940 --> 00:02:19,260
was to show that Jackson
was a serial paedophile.

43
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:21,060
However, Jackson's defence

44
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:25,180
claim he's being falsely accused
by a family after his money.

45
00:02:25,380 --> 00:02:27,020
Speaking to journalists
this morning,

46
00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:31,220
Michael Jackson's lawyer said
the pop star is denying all charges.

47
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:35,420
A trial in California will decide
who is right and who is wrong.

48
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:43,700
This morning, the whole world
is watching this small courthouse

49
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:47,500
in Santa Maria, a town
in the county of Santa Barbara,

50
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:49,660
in anticipation of what might be

51
00:02:49,860 --> 00:02:52,460
the biggest trial
we will ever witness.

52
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:54,940
Michael Jackson was,
at that time, quite simply,

53
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:56,860
the biggest entertainer,

54
00:02:57,060 --> 00:03:01,820
the most famous entertainer
the world had ever known.

55
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:03,580
And we were there for, what,

56
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:08,460
four long, long months,
covering this extraordinary trial.

57
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:11,300
It was a very exciting case
to cover,

58
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:15,640
in the sense of just the sheer
magnitude of the defendant.

59
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:19,980
I mean, we were talking
about a massive major megastar

60
00:03:20,180 --> 00:03:21,180
that the world loved.

61
00:03:21,380 --> 00:03:22,940
And the fans -

62
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:26,900
it was like a concert,
cos the fans were going crazy.

63
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:28,100
Look, this is court.

64
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:31,260
This is a felony charge
that can get him 20 years in prison.

65
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:35,660
But you felt, that first day,
it felt like a concert.

66
00:03:35,860 --> 00:03:38,380
We're talking about tents
and lights and cameras

67
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:40,860
and fans and protesters
and reporters.

68
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:44,820
I mean, it truly built
into a media circus.

69
00:03:45,020 --> 00:03:46,980
We love you more!

70
00:03:47,180 --> 00:03:52,180
This was an extraordinary tableau
of ridiculousness.

71
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:57,020
These Michael Jackson fans
moonwalking outside the court,

72
00:03:57,220 --> 00:03:58,500
impersonating Michael Jackson.

73
00:04:02,620 --> 00:04:07,980
People from all over the world
who come to this tiny town.

74
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:11,220
And for four months, it was bedlam.

75
00:04:11,420 --> 00:04:13,580
With the prosecution set
to open its case,

76
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:17,300
defendant Michael Jackson
makes his grand arrival.

77
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:21,900
I remember the first day, because
he had gotten The Nation of Islam

78
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:25,760
and their security team, and
they marched in ahead of Michael.

79
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:29,620
They marched down the street
as Michael's motorcade was coming.

80
00:04:29,820 --> 00:04:31,580
It was such a powerful sight.

81
00:04:35,860 --> 00:04:39,100
The first time I saw Michael Jackson
walk into the courtroom,

82
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:41,260
he looked terrified,

83
00:04:41,460 --> 00:04:46,780
and he was so thin
and just looked fragile

84
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:48,940
and just like
he was scared to death.

85
00:04:49,140 --> 00:04:52,980
Leading the prosecution
against Jackson is Tom Sneddon,

86
00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:55,380
who'd had dealings
with the pop star in the past.

87
00:04:55,580 --> 00:05:00,020
The lead prosecutor was the district
attorney for Santa Barbara,

88
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:03,300
who was a very experienced
criminal prosecutor.

89
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:06,580
Tom Sneddon
was a very well-known prosecutor,

90
00:05:06,780 --> 00:05:07,540
a very serious guy.

91
00:05:07,740 --> 00:05:12,660
He had been pursuing Michael Jackson
for years, at least a decade.

92
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:14,140
12 years earlier,

93
00:05:14,340 --> 00:05:17,520
the world was stunned
when Jackson faced allegations

94
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:20,700
of abusing another 13-year-old boy,
Jordan Chandler.

95
00:05:20,900 --> 00:05:25,300
Back then, Sneddon was unable
to criminally charge Jackson.

96
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:28,580
He tried it once before,
back in the early '90s.

97
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:30,740
That prosecution had failed.

98
00:05:30,940 --> 00:05:33,080
And you could really feel
from Tom Sneddon

99
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:35,420
the importance
of what this case brought.

100
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:38,100
Jackson is represented in court

101
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:41,300
by highly regarded defence attorney
Thomas Mesereau.

102
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:44,780
Tom Mesereau was one
of the top defence attorneys

103
00:05:44,980 --> 00:05:47,100
in America, hands down.

104
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:52,260
He did Mike Tyson, and later on,
he would come to do Bill Cosby.

105
00:05:52,460 --> 00:05:55,340
And he was a great attorney,
as simple as that.

106
00:05:55,540 --> 00:06:00,060
Thomas Mesereau had a very
commanding presence in the courtroom

107
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:04,780
and not only commanding presence,
but a calm about him, as well.

108
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:11,380
He was tall, and then his hair
was just solid snow white.

109
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:14,480
And he really knew
what he was talking about.

110
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:17,380
Mesereau and his team
have their work cut out

111
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:21,380
defending Jackson against
ten very serious charges.

112
00:06:23,980 --> 00:06:25,780
The prosecution's strategy
is to show

113
00:06:25,980 --> 00:06:29,480
that Michael Jackson was sleeping
in bed with little boys,

114
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:33,180
and that what he was doing was
illegal, that it was a felony,

115
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:34,780
and they wanted him convicted.

116
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:36,180
Good morning.

117
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:41,460
The private world of Michael Jackson
reveals that instead of cookies

118
00:06:41,660 --> 00:06:42,940
and instead of milk,

119
00:06:43,140 --> 00:06:47,460
you can substitute wine, vodka
and bourbon

120
00:06:47,660 --> 00:06:52,400
instead of children's
books and discussions of Peter Pan.

121
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:57,340
This 44-year-old man is sharing
with 13-year-old Gavin

122
00:06:57,540 --> 00:07:00,820
his collection
of sexually explicit magazines.

123
00:07:02,460 --> 00:07:05,220
You are going to be able to peek

124
00:07:05,420 --> 00:07:07,900
into the private world
of the defendant,

125
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:10,920
and you are going to hear from Gavin

126
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:13,940
as he describes to you
his molestation.

127
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:16,380
I sensed a bit of a kind

128
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:19,340
of a frustration or an anger,
you know,

129
00:07:19,540 --> 00:07:22,940
like he really...
he really was serious about this.

130
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:26,220
In court,
Jackson hardly said anything.

131
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:29,300
He occasionally spoke
to his lawyers,

132
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:31,700
but for most of the time,
he just sat there

133
00:07:31,900 --> 00:07:34,100
and had no expression
on his face at all.

134
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:42,940
I submit to you, we will prove
it never, ever happened.

135
00:07:43,140 --> 00:07:47,180
So many people around the world
want to get near him.

136
00:07:47,380 --> 00:07:49,620
People are always just buzzing
around him,

137
00:07:49,820 --> 00:07:51,300
trying to grab hold of something

138
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:54,060
that will give them
fame and fortune.

139
00:07:54,260 --> 00:07:58,500
It's an ongoing reality.
It's an ongoing problem.

140
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:02,500
There are many, many challenges
in defending

141
00:08:02,700 --> 00:08:03,860
in a case of that nature

142
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:07,060
that, when a young person
makes an allegation of sexual abuse,

143
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:08,220
the big question is

144
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:11,820
why would the individual do that
unless it was true?

145
00:08:12,020 --> 00:08:14,720
And obviously,
there's a lot of sympathy

146
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:17,620
that goes with an allegation
like that.

147
00:08:17,820 --> 00:08:19,060
I think there was a feeling

148
00:08:19,260 --> 00:08:22,500
that Michael Jackson
was gonna be found guilty.

149
00:08:24,740 --> 00:08:28,940
Michael's innocent!
Michael's innocent!

150
00:08:29,140 --> 00:08:31,700
Michael Jackson arriving
for the second day of his trial,

151
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:35,940
charged with the molestation of
former cancer victim Gavin Arvizo.

152
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:38,380
Today, the first
prosecution witnesses

153
00:08:38,580 --> 00:08:40,100
will begin giving evidence.

154
00:08:44,260 --> 00:08:46,700
The first witness
called by the prosecution

155
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:49,060
is British journalist Martin Bashir.

156
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:52,660
Three years earlier,
Bashir spent eight months

157
00:08:52,860 --> 00:08:55,700
filming a documentary called
Living With Michael Jackson.

158
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:58,740
And using your heel.
Use your heel to slide back.

159
00:08:58,940 --> 00:09:00,220
Slide back on your heel.

160
00:09:00,420 --> 00:09:04,020
Initially, the star was excited
about the film.

161
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:08,700
Michael calls, and he says,
"I have this huge thing coming out.

162
00:09:08,900 --> 00:09:10,460
"It's gonna change the world.

163
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:13,660
"It's gonna change
everybody's perception of me.

164
00:09:13,860 --> 00:09:15,220
"It's gonna be great."

165
00:09:15,420 --> 00:09:19,100
During filming, Bashir noticed
Jackson spending time

166
00:09:19,300 --> 00:09:21,700
with the 12-year-old
called Gavin Arvizo,

167
00:09:21,900 --> 00:09:23,860
and he interviewed them together.

168
00:09:24,060 --> 00:09:28,860
When people hear
that children stayed in your bedroom

169
00:09:29,060 --> 00:09:31,940
and they say,
"Is that really appropriate

170
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:35,020
"for a man, a grown man,
to be doing that?",

171
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:36,340
how do you respond to that?

172
00:09:36,540 --> 00:09:37,300
I feel sorry for them,

173
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:41,140
because that's judging someone
who wants to really help people.

174
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:42,700
Why can't you share your bed?

175
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:48,300
The most loving thing to do
is to share your bed with someone.

176
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:51,180
It proved to be catastrophic
for the singer.

177
00:09:51,380 --> 00:09:55,760
Documentary drops on ABC
in February,

178
00:09:55,960 --> 00:10:00,140
and it was a disaster
from the word go.

179
00:10:00,340 --> 00:10:05,700
Jackson is seen in that documentary
holding hands with Gavin Arvizo.

180
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:10,380
He also talked about sleepovers
with young children.

181
00:10:10,580 --> 00:10:15,060
The little boy was leaning
on Michael's shoulder.

182
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:17,740
There was clearly affection there.

183
00:10:17,940 --> 00:10:20,220
A little too close for comfort.

184
00:10:20,420 --> 00:10:25,880
And that was what clearly proved
so inflammatory.

185
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:31,540
The effect of that documentary
was extraordinary.

186
00:10:31,740 --> 00:10:34,260
Gavin Arvizo
had been battling cancer

187
00:10:34,460 --> 00:10:37,380
when he was introduced
to Michael Jackson in hospital.

188
00:10:37,580 --> 00:10:40,260
The star invited his family
to Neverland,

189
00:10:40,460 --> 00:10:41,980
and they became friends.

190
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:46,060
After the jury is shown
his documentary,

191
00:10:46,260 --> 00:10:47,740
the prosecution questioned Bashir.

192
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:52,780
The prosecution needed to call him
in order to exhibit the documentary

193
00:10:52,980 --> 00:10:55,860
that had been the trigger
for the whole investigation.

194
00:10:56,060 --> 00:10:59,620
Mr Bashir, what is
your profession or occupation?

195
00:10:59,820 --> 00:11:03,180
I've been involved
in journalism for 20 years,

196
00:11:03,380 --> 00:11:06,100
and I've been a television
journalist for around 18 years.

197
00:11:07,260 --> 00:11:11,020
Martin Bashir is happy to answer
questions from the prosecution,

198
00:11:11,220 --> 00:11:14,380
but in cross-examination,
he's less forthcoming.

199
00:11:16,540 --> 00:11:19,380
What I think Thomas Mesereau
desperately wanted to get into

200
00:11:19,580 --> 00:11:23,760
was the tactics
that Martin Bashir employed

201
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:27,940
in order to get people
to open up to him -

202
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:33,260
the fact that he would insinuate
himself into people's trust

203
00:11:33,460 --> 00:11:36,060
and then basically turn on them.

204
00:11:36,260 --> 00:11:37,700
Mr Bashir,

205
00:11:37,900 --> 00:11:41,860
in the process of attempting to
obtain statements from Mr Jackson,

206
00:11:42,060 --> 00:11:44,940
you called him "the boss",
didn't you?

207
00:11:46,540 --> 00:11:51,540
Did you want to answer that?
I don't, Your Honour.

208
00:11:51,740 --> 00:11:55,780
Mr Bashir clammed up
and refused to answer questions

209
00:11:55,980 --> 00:12:00,020
from Jackson's defence attorney,
Thomas Mesereau.

210
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:02,780
Mr Bashir, to prepare,

211
00:12:02,980 --> 00:12:06,540
the show you've just shown the jury
in this courtroom,

212
00:12:06,740 --> 00:12:09,300
you told them you had
an abiding sense

213
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:12,980
that he is a selfless
and most generous person.

214
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:15,500
Correct?

215
00:12:17,140 --> 00:12:20,300
Do you wanna answer that question?
I don't, Your Honour.

216
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:26,860
He relied almost entirely on
the right of journalistic privilege

217
00:12:27,060 --> 00:12:29,340
in declining to answer questions.

218
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:34,400
Thomas Mesereau and, indeed,
his client, Michael Jackson,

219
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:39,460
clearly believed
that the film fatally misrepresented

220
00:12:39,660 --> 00:12:41,700
who Michael Jackson was.

221
00:12:41,900 --> 00:12:46,380
Michael was very upset
by the way he was portrayed.

222
00:12:46,580 --> 00:12:48,780
He felt this wasn't
a true depiction of him.

223
00:12:48,980 --> 00:12:54,220
So he had one of his videographers
film over what Bashir was filming

224
00:12:54,420 --> 00:12:55,820
when he was filming the interview.

225
00:12:56,020 --> 00:12:59,140
Two weeks
after the Bashir film aired,

226
00:12:59,340 --> 00:13:02,580
Jackson broadcast his own version
in retaliation.

227
00:13:02,780 --> 00:13:08,140
It features footage his team filmed
of scenes Bashir edited out.

228
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:12,980
I love them.

229
00:13:22,660 --> 00:13:23,660
Thank you so much.

230
00:13:23,860 --> 00:13:27,180
The boy with Jackson
in the Bashir documentary,

231
00:13:27,380 --> 00:13:30,380
Gavin Arvizo,
was also filmed with his family.

232
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:33,580
Vincent Amen was involved
in the production.

233
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:35,820
I was told that the Arvizos
were gonna

234
00:13:36,020 --> 00:13:40,100
be doing a video deposition
of their relationship -

235
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:42,680
true relationship -
with Michael Jackson.

236
00:13:42,880 --> 00:13:45,260
We now know it
as the video rebuttal,

237
00:13:45,460 --> 00:13:47,420
as it was called during trial.

238
00:13:47,620 --> 00:13:49,780
In this rebuttal video,
you have Gavin

239
00:13:49,980 --> 00:13:52,560
and his sister, Davellin
and mom, Janet, and Star,

240
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:55,140
and everybody is talking
about singing his praises,

241
00:13:55,340 --> 00:13:58,500
literally talking about
how great he is and how, you know,

242
00:13:58,700 --> 00:14:00,780
none of this
could have ever happened

243
00:14:00,980 --> 00:14:01,460
and they loved him.

244
00:14:01,660 --> 00:14:05,020
The first impression was
Janet was not happy at the time.

245
00:14:05,220 --> 00:14:08,180
She felt bad for Michael.

246
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:10,540
And this was a mischaracterisation
of Michael

247
00:14:10,740 --> 00:14:14,740
and a mischaracterisation of
Gavin's relationship with Michael.

248
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:19,200
I gave my brother the extra
little spark he needed in his mind,

249
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:23,660
cos my brother was to the point
where he couldn't even move.

250
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:25,860
He couldn't even... talk.

251
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:31,140
And he gave
my little brother so much.

252
00:14:32,340 --> 00:14:33,420
I was generally moved.

253
00:14:33,620 --> 00:14:37,060
I felt this was
an ethical production,

254
00:14:37,260 --> 00:14:40,380
a very truthful production.

255
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:45,740
And it actually moved me
to believe the Arvizo family

256
00:14:45,940 --> 00:14:48,260
and their relationship
to Michael Jackson

257
00:14:48,460 --> 00:14:50,780
and basically cleared up
any doubt that I had

258
00:14:50,980 --> 00:14:52,660
in Michael Jackson's innocence.

259
00:14:52,860 --> 00:14:56,820
The rebuttal video seems like
perfect evidence for the defence.

260
00:14:57,020 --> 00:14:59,220
However,
in a surprise turn of events,

261
00:14:59,420 --> 00:15:03,660
the interview is presented
in court by the prosecution.

262
00:15:05,500 --> 00:15:08,860
In reality, according
to prosecutors, this was fiction.

263
00:15:09,060 --> 00:15:12,180
It wasn't reality.
They were told they had to do it.

264
00:15:12,380 --> 00:15:15,300
They needed to do it.
They'd been given so much.

265
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:19,320
Michael Jackson, according
to other accusers, would say,

266
00:15:19,520 --> 00:15:23,340
"If you tell what we have done,
we're both going to jail.

267
00:15:23,540 --> 00:15:24,860
"We're going to be in trouble."

268
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:30,140
Before long, Gavin's mum
dramatically turned on Jackson,

269
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:34,460
alleging sexual abuse of her son,
and even kidnap.

270
00:15:34,660 --> 00:15:35,540
Following her complaint,

271
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:40,940
70 police officers raid Neverland
in search of incriminating evidence

272
00:15:41,140 --> 00:15:44,100
and, a short time later,
Jackson was arrested.

273
00:15:47,300 --> 00:15:52,500
Gavin's 18-year-old sister Davellin,
who appears in the rebuttal video,

274
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:55,780
is the first family member
called by the prosecution.

275
00:15:55,980 --> 00:15:59,460
Davellin, the sister,
said in her evidence

276
00:15:59,660 --> 00:16:02,260
that they had been given a script.

277
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:03,940
Sneddon asked her...

278
00:16:04,140 --> 00:16:06,020
What did he say about the rebuttal?

279
00:16:06,220 --> 00:16:09,020
It was just we were supposed
to say nice things about him,

280
00:16:09,220 --> 00:16:12,260
and he offered us a piece of paper.

281
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:15,300
Paper? What do you mean by a paper?

282
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:18,980
Kind of like a script.
Do you remember what was on it?

283
00:16:19,180 --> 00:16:21,900
Just nice things of Mr Jackson,
and that's it.

284
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:23,540
The effect of her testimony

285
00:16:23,740 --> 00:16:29,980
was that the rebuttal video
was pre-scripted

286
00:16:30,180 --> 00:16:35,460
in order to paint the most positive
light you could have of Michael.

287
00:16:35,660 --> 00:16:40,940
Davellin did not witness the central
accusation of alleged molestation.

288
00:16:41,140 --> 00:16:45,340
But in her testimony, other
disturbing behaviour comes to light.

289
00:16:45,540 --> 00:16:50,980
On the stand, Davellin,
the older sister, mentioned,

290
00:16:51,180 --> 00:16:55,780
among other things, that she and her
siblings had been served alcohol.

291
00:16:57,180 --> 00:16:59,060
You've got the idea
of Michael Jackson

292
00:16:59,260 --> 00:17:01,740
pouring red wine into a soda can

293
00:17:01,940 --> 00:17:05,220
and then giving it to a child
and calling it Jesus juice,

294
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:08,780
like Jesus drank the red wine
with his disciples.

295
00:17:08,980 --> 00:17:12,900
This megastar is taking red wine and
pouring it into an empty coke can

296
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:14,580
to give to a kid.

297
00:17:14,780 --> 00:17:16,060
That's what is being told to us,

298
00:17:16,260 --> 00:17:18,420
and so you have
to visualise that happening.

299
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:22,720
And at first it seems like
"No way! Did that happen?"

300
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:26,820
It seems
to kind of stun some people.

301
00:17:27,020 --> 00:17:32,700
What I saw, anyway, is a couple
of the jurors looking at him

302
00:17:32,900 --> 00:17:36,100
like a little bit,
"OK, I'm disappointed in you.

303
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:37,460
"I'm a little angry."

304
00:17:37,660 --> 00:17:39,100
And I think the prosecution felt

305
00:17:39,300 --> 00:17:42,060
like they won
some big points with that.

306
00:17:42,260 --> 00:17:45,020
Yet alcohol is only the tip
of the iceberg.

307
00:17:47,860 --> 00:17:51,540
Next, the prosecution calls
Gavin's younger brother, Star,

308
00:17:51,740 --> 00:17:54,100
who has even more
disturbing revelations

309
00:17:54,300 --> 00:17:56,980
of what went on behind closed doors.

310
00:17:57,180 --> 00:18:00,980
We heard about pornography,
that pornography was in the house,

311
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:03,740
that it was out, that it was shared,
that it was viewed,

312
00:18:03,940 --> 00:18:07,660
that, you know, it was something
that they all looked at together.

313
00:18:07,860 --> 00:18:12,100
"Do you recall whose idea it was
to go on the internet?"

314
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:13,220
"Michael's.

315
00:18:13,420 --> 00:18:15,260
"While we were on
one of those sites,

316
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:20,020
"a lady had her shirt up,
and Michael said, 'Got milk?'

317
00:18:20,220 --> 00:18:22,180
"Yeah, and then
he leaned over to Prince,

318
00:18:22,380 --> 00:18:26,700
"and he says,
'You're missing some P-U-S-S-Y.' "

319
00:18:26,900 --> 00:18:31,420
How many sites do you feel
that you went to that night?

320
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:36,140
I don't really remember,
but probably, say, five or six.

321
00:18:36,340 --> 00:18:38,300
And what did those sites have?

322
00:18:38,500 --> 00:18:41,260
You don't need to go
into all of the details,

323
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:44,220
but generally,
what was their common denominator?

324
00:18:44,420 --> 00:18:45,980
Females.

325
00:18:46,180 --> 00:18:49,580
The alcohol and the pornography
is important evidence

326
00:18:49,780 --> 00:18:50,700
for the prosecution.

327
00:18:50,900 --> 00:18:54,660
But Star has something
much more serious to reveal.

328
00:18:54,860 --> 00:18:59,220
And it's the first time
this evidence is heard.

329
00:18:59,420 --> 00:19:03,580
The bombshell moment
of Star Arvizo's evidence

330
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:08,400
came when he claimed
to have seen his brother Gavin

331
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:13,090
on a bed at Neverland Ranch
with Michael Jackson.

332
00:19:13,290 --> 00:19:17,580
I think the gist of it
was that Star observed

333
00:19:17,780 --> 00:19:23,020
Michael Jackson sexually abusing
his brother Gavin.

334
00:19:23,220 --> 00:19:26,220
You said you saw his hands.

335
00:19:26,420 --> 00:19:29,300
Whose hands were you talking about?

336
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:32,380
Michael's.
And where were his hands?

337
00:19:32,580 --> 00:19:35,460
His left hand
was in my brother's pants,

338
00:19:35,660 --> 00:19:37,940
and the right hand was in HIS pants.

339
00:19:39,620 --> 00:19:44,180
Did you see, if anything,
what he was doing?

340
00:19:44,380 --> 00:19:46,540
He was masturbating.

341
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:52,220
That was the first and, indeed,

342
00:19:52,420 --> 00:19:56,060
the only direct eye witness account

343
00:19:56,260 --> 00:19:58,540
of alleged molestation.

344
00:19:58,740 --> 00:20:00,100
And what does that tell you?

345
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:03,140
This is a kid looking at something
happening to his own brother.

346
00:20:07,260 --> 00:20:08,660
Seems clear to me.

347
00:20:08,860 --> 00:20:13,820
He witnessed his brother being,
I guess, molested by Michael.

348
00:20:14,020 --> 00:20:17,660
And when you have a eyewitness,

349
00:20:17,860 --> 00:20:21,820
that seems to be game, set, match -
trial's over, you're guilty.

350
00:20:22,020 --> 00:20:24,780
It's amazing to me that the jury,
having heard that...

351
00:20:26,020 --> 00:20:29,420
..did not, at least in their minds,
convict him right then and there.

352
00:20:30,620 --> 00:20:32,460
I mean,
how much more evidence do you need?

353
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:37,400
Star's testimony
is undeniably powerful.

354
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:40,380
However, the defence strategy
from the start

355
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:43,540
is to undermine the prosecution case
and its witnesses.

356
00:20:47,300 --> 00:20:50,020
You didn't immediately go
to your mother and report that,

357
00:20:50,220 --> 00:20:51,580
did you, when you saw it?

358
00:20:51,780 --> 00:20:52,940
No.

359
00:20:53,140 --> 00:20:55,980
You didn't immediately go to
your father and report that, right?

360
00:20:56,180 --> 00:20:57,460
My dad wasn't there.

361
00:20:57,660 --> 00:21:00,500
You didn't immediately
tell Davellin about it, right?

362
00:21:00,700 --> 00:21:01,940
No.

363
00:21:02,140 --> 00:21:04,940
Now you've indicated -
for the first time ever -

364
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:09,140
discussed any alleged inappropriate
touching by Michael Jackson

365
00:21:09,340 --> 00:21:12,060
was with psychologist Stanley Katz,
right?

366
00:21:12,260 --> 00:21:13,980
Yes.

367
00:21:14,180 --> 00:21:17,900
And you've admitted that you gave
Stanley Katz a different description

368
00:21:18,100 --> 00:21:20,340
than you've given
in this courtroom, right?

369
00:21:20,540 --> 00:21:21,420
Yes.

370
00:21:22,580 --> 00:21:25,140
In fact, you never mentioned
the third event

371
00:21:25,340 --> 00:21:27,900
that you've described today
to Stanley Katz.

372
00:21:28,100 --> 00:21:30,100
Because I might have forgot
about it.

373
00:21:32,740 --> 00:21:33,820
What Mesereau did with Star

374
00:21:34,020 --> 00:21:37,400
was he tried to point out
inconsistencies in his stories.

375
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:41,390
And so, the more that you
can paint an inconsistent story

376
00:21:41,590 --> 00:21:45,380
from a witness, then that gives
reasonable doubt for jurors.

377
00:21:45,580 --> 00:21:47,940
And that's what
the defence is always trying to do

378
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:50,940
to get to that reasonable doubt.

379
00:21:51,140 --> 00:21:52,300
In the rebuttal video,

380
00:21:52,500 --> 00:21:55,020
which the family claim
was scripted and false,

381
00:21:55,220 --> 00:21:58,040
Star praised Jackson
as a father figure.

382
00:21:58,240 --> 00:22:00,860
Defence counsel
asked the following -

383
00:22:01,060 --> 00:22:04,580
"Star, do you remember making those
comments about Michael Jackson?"

384
00:22:04,780 --> 00:22:06,980
Sure.
Were you telling the truth?

385
00:22:10,700 --> 00:22:13,340
No, not really.

386
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:16,540
Were you lying?
Yeah.

387
00:22:16,740 --> 00:22:18,340
On there, yes.

388
00:22:18,540 --> 00:22:24,260
So you were lying when you said
Michael let you feel like his son.

389
00:22:24,460 --> 00:22:27,660
You weren't telling the truth?
Yes.

390
00:22:27,860 --> 00:22:30,700
And when you said
he let you call him father,

391
00:22:30,900 --> 00:22:32,980
you weren't telling the truth?

392
00:22:33,180 --> 00:22:34,380
Yes.

393
00:22:34,580 --> 00:22:37,340
Defence counsel is demonstrating

394
00:22:37,540 --> 00:22:40,900
that Star had lied
on previous occasions.

395
00:22:41,100 --> 00:22:43,520
And that's a very, very
significant development.

396
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:46,140
You've got the statements
in the rebuttal video,

397
00:22:46,340 --> 00:22:48,260
you've got what we're hearing
on the stand.

398
00:22:48,460 --> 00:22:50,380
Some of the time,
it's two different things.

399
00:22:50,580 --> 00:22:51,420
Which one was it?

400
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:54,260
And some of these stories
are inconsistent.

401
00:22:54,460 --> 00:22:57,240
The defence strategy seems
to be working.

402
00:22:57,440 --> 00:23:00,220
However, next comes
their biggest challenge

403
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:02,060
as the accuser
is called to testify...

404
00:23:02,260 --> 00:23:07,580
He started acting like he was having
sex with the mannequin.

405
00:23:07,780 --> 00:23:11,660
..not, though, before
the court is thrown into chaos.

406
00:23:11,860 --> 00:23:15,740
This was the circus,
and this was another day in it.

407
00:23:16,740 --> 00:23:19,820
It is the second week
of the Michael Jackson trial,

408
00:23:20,020 --> 00:23:23,180
and the prosecution has called
the main accuser, Gavin Arvizo,

409
00:23:23,380 --> 00:23:24,660
to give evidence.

410
00:23:24,860 --> 00:23:27,420
This is
the star witness of the case.

411
00:23:27,620 --> 00:23:30,660
This is Gavin on the stand
to tell his story.

412
00:23:30,860 --> 00:23:33,700
This is the accuser
facing Michael Jackson.

413
00:23:33,900 --> 00:23:38,300
Tom Sneddon would have realised,
as an experienced prosecutor,

414
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:41,500
this was the most important part
of his case.

415
00:23:41,700 --> 00:23:46,180
He had to present Gavin
as a credible witness to the jury,

416
00:23:46,380 --> 00:23:48,100
otherwise his case would fail.

417
00:23:49,380 --> 00:23:53,060
And when it's a child,
it's a particularly daunting

418
00:23:53,260 --> 00:23:56,940
and complicated and challenging
state of affairs.

419
00:24:01,820 --> 00:24:04,980
However,
on the day Gavin, now 15,

420
00:24:05,180 --> 00:24:07,500
is due to talk
about the alleged abuse,

421
00:24:07,700 --> 00:24:10,020
the court is suddenly thrown
into chaos.

422
00:24:11,620 --> 00:24:14,180
We're talking
about high-stakes drama.

423
00:24:14,380 --> 00:24:17,540
This is the moment
that everybody is waiting for.

424
00:24:17,740 --> 00:24:18,820
What's gonna happen?

425
00:24:19,020 --> 00:24:23,740
And then you've got this entirely
different scenario that unfolds.

426
00:24:23,940 --> 00:24:28,660
We all settle into court,
and then there's no Michael Jackson.

427
00:24:28,860 --> 00:24:31,700
Where is the famous defendant?

428
00:24:31,900 --> 00:24:35,260
That's what the judge,
Judge Melville, wanted to know.

429
00:24:35,460 --> 00:24:41,820
And as the clock... clock ticked,
no sign of Jackson whatsoever.

430
00:24:42,020 --> 00:24:44,500
So Judge Melville was very upset.

431
00:24:44,700 --> 00:24:47,980
I notice
the defendant's not present.

432
00:24:48,180 --> 00:24:49,660
Yes, Your Honour.

433
00:24:49,860 --> 00:24:53,140
Mr Jackson is at Cottage Hospital
in Santa Ynez

434
00:24:53,340 --> 00:24:54,740
with a serious back problem.

435
00:24:54,940 --> 00:24:58,380
We are all standing out there.
I'm outside now, right?

436
00:24:58,580 --> 00:25:01,080
And, you know,
we were gonna go live.

437
00:25:01,280 --> 00:25:03,580
Breaking news -
Michael Jackson is gone.

438
00:25:03,780 --> 00:25:07,340
I mean, of all the days, this is
the day everybody wants to see.

439
00:25:07,540 --> 00:25:09,500
They want to see him
come through that door,

440
00:25:09,700 --> 00:25:12,940
take his seat inside the courtroom
and face his accuser.

441
00:25:13,140 --> 00:25:14,060
This is the moment.

442
00:25:14,260 --> 00:25:17,740
I'm going to issue a warrant
for his arrest.

443
00:25:17,940 --> 00:25:20,220
I'm forfeiting his bail,

444
00:25:20,420 --> 00:25:23,820
and I will hold that order
for one hour.

445
00:25:24,020 --> 00:25:27,420
In one hour,
I will execute that order.

446
00:25:27,620 --> 00:25:28,780
If your bail is revoked.

447
00:25:28,980 --> 00:25:32,660
you go behind bars
for the duration of the trial.

448
00:25:32,860 --> 00:25:35,500
And that was what he was facing
at the time.

449
00:25:35,700 --> 00:25:39,540
Mesereau is forced to make
a desperate call to his client

450
00:25:39,740 --> 00:25:41,860
and insist
Jackson returns immediately.

451
00:25:42,060 --> 00:25:44,980
When, an hour later,
the singer finally appears,

452
00:25:45,180 --> 00:25:47,940
no-one can quite believe their eyes.

453
00:25:48,140 --> 00:25:49,380
When he did turn up,

454
00:25:49,580 --> 00:25:54,820
Jackson walked into court
in his pyjama bottoms.

455
00:25:55,020 --> 00:25:58,740
See, I'm thinking,
"What in the world is going on here?

456
00:25:58,940 --> 00:26:03,940
"Is he crazy? Has he lost it?
Has he totally gone bonkers here?"

457
00:26:04,140 --> 00:26:08,980
And he's walking,
like, so slow and gingerly, and...

458
00:26:09,180 --> 00:26:13,580
and I'm saying, "OK, this is...
this is bad, this is really bad."

459
00:26:13,780 --> 00:26:15,820
It was just a crazy moment,
because it's not often

460
00:26:16,020 --> 00:26:19,340
that you see a defendant walking
into court wearing pyjamas.

461
00:26:19,540 --> 00:26:21,800
But listen, this was the circus,

462
00:26:22,000 --> 00:26:24,260
and this was another day in it.

463
00:26:26,540 --> 00:26:27,780
It was certainly speculated

464
00:26:27,980 --> 00:26:31,140
that the reason that he had to go
to the hospital suddenly

465
00:26:31,340 --> 00:26:34,500
for back pain was because
he didn't wanna face his accuser.

466
00:26:34,700 --> 00:26:35,780
That's what it felt like.

467
00:26:35,980 --> 00:26:39,940
Jackson now has to hear
the most serious allegations

468
00:26:40,140 --> 00:26:42,860
from his accuser in his pyjamas.

469
00:26:43,900 --> 00:26:45,540
Sneddon asked Gavin

470
00:26:45,740 --> 00:26:49,460
about a mannequin Jackson had
in his bedroom.

471
00:26:49,660 --> 00:26:54,220
Did you ever see Mr Jackson
do anything with that mannequin?

472
00:26:55,420 --> 00:26:56,540
Yes.

473
00:26:57,620 --> 00:27:02,940
He started acting like he was
having sex with the mannequin.

474
00:27:03,140 --> 00:27:06,500
So, what did he do
with the mannequin?

475
00:27:06,700 --> 00:27:08,660
He acted like he was humping it.

476
00:27:08,860 --> 00:27:11,540
And where was he
when he was doing this?

477
00:27:11,740 --> 00:27:12,940
On the bed.

478
00:27:14,380 --> 00:27:15,900
According to Gavin,

479
00:27:16,100 --> 00:27:19,980
the singer pressurised him
to engage in sexual activity.

480
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:21,260
What did he say to you?

481
00:27:21,460 --> 00:27:24,660
He said that
if men don't masturbate,

482
00:27:24,860 --> 00:27:28,700
they might rape a girl
or be kind of unstable.

483
00:27:32,100 --> 00:27:35,060
The jury has already heard
about the alleged abuse

484
00:27:35,260 --> 00:27:36,500
from Gavin's younger brother, Star.

485
00:27:36,700 --> 00:27:40,100
Now it's time to hear it
from the accuser.

486
00:27:40,300 --> 00:27:41,620
This is the crucial evidence

487
00:27:41,820 --> 00:27:45,020
from the most important witness
in the case.

488
00:27:45,220 --> 00:27:47,300
This is Gavin on the stand.

489
00:27:47,500 --> 00:27:50,740
So, he says, "And then so he..."

490
00:27:50,940 --> 00:27:54,580
"We were under the covers,
and I had his pyjamas on,

491
