00:41:54,580 --> 00:41:58,180
At the time,
I hadn't slept for so long.

741
00:41:59,420 --> 00:42:02,380
And everyone was asleep.

742
00:42:02,580 --> 00:42:04,460
And it was hours into the flight.

743
00:42:04,660 --> 00:42:06,740
She describes an incident

744
00:42:06,940 --> 00:42:10,180
involving Michael Jackson
and her son on board a private jet.

745
00:42:11,780 --> 00:42:13,940
I figured this was my chance

746
00:42:14,140 --> 00:42:18,460
to go and check to see
what was going on back there, and...

747
00:42:19,700 --> 00:42:24,020
..that's when I saw Michael licking
Gavin's head.

748
00:42:25,700 --> 00:42:27,100
And I... I thought it was me.

749
00:42:27,300 --> 00:42:29,500
I thought I was seeing things,
I thought it was me.

750
00:42:32,180 --> 00:42:33,900
That's the sketch I drew,

751
00:42:34,100 --> 00:42:38,300
was of Janet going... like that

752
00:42:38,500 --> 00:42:43,700
to show how Michael was licking
Gavin's head.

753
00:42:43,900 --> 00:42:45,900
People called her combative
at times,

754
00:42:46,100 --> 00:42:49,140
and there were some times
where she did these snap moves,

755
00:42:49,340 --> 00:42:52,980
where you were just taken aback
in the courtroom,

756
00:42:53,180 --> 00:42:54,860
and you could see
the physical reaction

757
00:42:55,060 --> 00:42:56,300
that some of the jurors had.

758
00:42:56,500 --> 00:42:59,100
You know, that's just not
typical behaviour of a witness.

759
00:42:59,300 --> 00:43:03,140
I don't think that people felt like
it went over well with the jury.

760
00:43:03,340 --> 00:43:07,660
She was very animated,
and it wasn't in a good way.

761
00:43:07,860 --> 00:43:08,940
It was astonishing, really.

762
00:43:09,140 --> 00:43:15,140
I mean, she just did not seem
a credible witness at all.

763
00:43:15,340 --> 00:43:17,700
She faltered. She prevaricated.

764
00:43:17,900 --> 00:43:20,900
She pointed her fingers at the jury.

765
00:43:21,100 --> 00:43:22,820
She lost her train of thought.

766
00:43:23,020 --> 00:43:27,420
She was the...
the ultimate unreliable witness.

767
00:43:27,620 --> 00:43:29,820
It was very sad,
cos, you know, she...

768
00:43:30,020 --> 00:43:32,220
that... that didn't look good
for her.

769
00:43:33,380 --> 00:43:36,240
By the time the prosecution
has finished questioning Janet,

770
00:43:36,440 --> 00:43:39,300
there is a feeling she has been
something of an own goal.

771
00:43:41,140 --> 00:43:45,060
So when Mesereau gets to his feet,
he smells blood.

772
00:43:49,980 --> 00:43:53,180
Mesereau's first point of attack
is Janet's claim

773
00:43:53,380 --> 00:43:56,420
that she and the children
were held captive at Neverland

774
00:43:56,620 --> 00:43:59,540
after their relationship
with Jackson broke down.

775
00:43:59,740 --> 00:44:03,020
Did you think you were being held
against your will by Mr Jackson

776
00:44:03,220 --> 00:44:05,100
or anyone associated with him?

777
00:44:05,300 --> 00:44:07,380
Did I think it?
Yes.

778
00:44:07,580 --> 00:44:09,220
I knew it.

779
00:44:09,420 --> 00:44:11,580
And did you think
you were the victim

780
00:44:11,780 --> 00:44:15,220
of either force or fear created by
anyone associated with Mr Jackson?

781
00:44:15,420 --> 00:44:16,500
I knew it.

782
00:44:16,700 --> 00:44:21,420
Yet you never went to court
to get a restraining order

783
00:44:21,620 --> 00:44:24,500
at any time
regarding Mr Jackson - true?

784
00:44:24,700 --> 00:44:26,020
I was too scared of him.

785
00:44:27,620 --> 00:44:31,460
The defence attorney is suggesting
Janet's testimony does not add up.

786
00:44:33,020 --> 00:44:35,300
Yes, the two of them
did not care for each other.

787
00:44:36,580 --> 00:44:39,720
And, uh, yeah,
Thomas Mesereau and her,

788
00:44:39,920 --> 00:44:42,860
when it was on cross-examination,
she...

789
00:44:43,060 --> 00:44:46,660
she was not liking the questions
he was asking.

790
00:44:46,860 --> 00:44:49,760
I felt that she was no match
for Tom Mesereau -

791
00:44:49,960 --> 00:44:52,850
not that many people
are a match for Tom Mesereau -

792
00:44:53,050 --> 00:44:55,740
but she was absolutely gonna be
out of her league.

793
00:44:55,940 --> 00:44:59,700
And I think that the prosecution
was wary of that, too.

794
00:44:59,900 --> 00:45:02,460
Janet becomes more irritated

795
00:45:02,660 --> 00:45:05,580
when defence attorney Mesereau
turns his attention

796
00:45:05,780 --> 00:45:08,660
to her claims of acting
in the rebuttal video.

797
00:45:08,860 --> 00:45:11,740
Well, you're correct.
I did an inadequate job.

798
00:45:11,940 --> 00:45:14,180
I'm a poor actress. You're right.

799
00:45:14,380 --> 00:45:16,260
I think you're a good one.

800
00:45:16,460 --> 00:45:17,740
"Oh, I think you're a good actress."

801
00:45:17,940 --> 00:45:22,340
You know, when he takes that tone,
you can feel his disdain.

802
00:45:22,540 --> 00:45:24,500
You know, you can feel it
in the courtroom

803
00:45:24,700 --> 00:45:27,780
that he doesn't like her,
he doesn't believe her.

804
00:45:27,980 --> 00:45:32,300
And he wants the jury to also call
into question her credibility.

805
00:45:32,500 --> 00:45:34,540
This is Thomas Mesereau

806
00:45:34,740 --> 00:45:40,060
basically lampooning Janet Arvizo
to highlight

807
00:45:40,260 --> 00:45:45,820
what an extraordinarily bad witness
for the prosecution she has been.

808
00:45:46,020 --> 00:45:49,540
He's having a bit of humour,
really, for the jury's benefit.

809
00:45:49,740 --> 00:45:53,140
Do you want me to shut
this trial down this afternoon?

810
00:45:53,340 --> 00:45:55,060
No, Your Honour, I don't.

811
00:45:55,260 --> 00:45:58,980
Then let's start taking this
seriously and act correctly.

812
00:45:59,180 --> 00:46:00,660
Yes, Your Honour.

813
00:46:00,860 --> 00:46:01,820
Go ahead.

814
00:46:03,140 --> 00:46:08,100
Mesereau might be toying with Janet
at times in his cross-examination,

815
00:46:08,300 --> 00:46:10,660
but he also wants to land
a knockout punch.

816
00:46:12,220 --> 00:46:14,700
There was a case in 1998
where Janet Arvizo

817
00:46:14,900 --> 00:46:18,900
claimed she'd been assaulted
by security officers from JCPenney,

818
00:46:19,100 --> 00:46:22,980
the store, where she was shown
to have lied,

819
00:46:23,180 --> 00:46:27,060
and where her and her family
had been awarded,

820
00:46:27,260 --> 00:46:29,560
I think, in excess of £150,000.

821
00:46:29,760 --> 00:46:31,860
The family was in the store

822
00:46:32,060 --> 00:46:34,420
when the children
had been suspected of shoplifting.

823
00:46:34,620 --> 00:46:38,220
In the car park, security guards
confronted Janet and her family.

824
00:46:38,420 --> 00:46:42,140
A fight ensued, and she claimed
she received injuries.

825
00:46:42,340 --> 00:46:43,880
So, she claimed that these injuries

826
00:46:44,080 --> 00:46:45,620
had been inflicted
by security guards,

827
00:46:45,820 --> 00:46:46,740
but she'd failed to accept

828
00:46:46,940 --> 00:46:50,700
that her husband
sometimes beat her up as well.

829
00:46:50,900 --> 00:46:52,860
In her testimony to the police,

830
00:46:53,060 --> 00:46:55,700
she claimed that
her husband had never beaten her up,

831
00:46:55,900 --> 00:46:58,140
something she later retracted.

832
00:46:58,340 --> 00:47:00,260
You told the Los Angeles
Police Department

833
00:47:00,460 --> 00:47:02,940
that for approximately 17 years

834
00:47:03,140 --> 00:47:06,140
he'd been physically
and emotionally abusing you, right?

835
00:47:06,340 --> 00:47:07,140
This is correct.

836
00:47:08,460 --> 00:47:12,060
But in the JCPenney case,
when you wanted money...

837
00:47:13,900 --> 00:47:16,700
..you said the opposite about David,
didn't you?

838
00:47:16,900 --> 00:47:19,340
So, Tom Mesereau
asks Janet on the stand,

839
00:47:19,540 --> 00:47:21,980
"You were not telling the truth
under oath

840
00:47:22,180 --> 00:47:23,380
"when you made those statements."

841
00:47:25,300 --> 00:47:27,180
The problem you had is

842
00:47:27,380 --> 00:47:31,520
that when you made allegations
later on

843
00:47:31,720 --> 00:47:35,660
regarding David abusing you
for 17 years,

844
00:47:35,860 --> 00:47:38,220
there's a deposition
that previously had been taken

845
00:47:38,420 --> 00:47:41,300
where you said the opposite
under oath.

846
00:47:41,500 --> 00:47:42,220
Correct?

847
00:47:42,420 --> 00:47:45,500
You're... It's too long.

848
00:47:45,700 --> 00:47:48,660
It's a yes and a no
and a yes and a no.

849
00:47:48,860 --> 00:47:50,020
And now I don't know.

850
00:47:53,020 --> 00:47:55,340
So she lied under oath
in the JCPenney's case.

851
00:47:55,540 --> 00:47:57,020
Is she lying under oath now?

852
00:47:57,220 --> 00:48:01,540
That is a big question being put
to jurors in this exchange.

853
00:48:01,740 --> 00:48:04,140
When a witness admits lying,

854
00:48:04,340 --> 00:48:08,340
this is always
an important stage of a trial.

855
00:48:08,540 --> 00:48:12,800
The impact of that revelation,
that admission,

856
00:48:13,000 --> 00:48:16,950
was devastating
to Janet Avizo's testimony

857
00:48:17,150 --> 00:48:21,100
because it basically portrayed her
as a liar,

858
00:48:21,300 --> 00:48:24,020
somebody who would lie for money.

859
00:48:24,220 --> 00:48:28,620
The mother of the accuser has failed
to deliver for the prosecution,

860
00:48:28,820 --> 00:48:32,300
so Sneddon and Zonen decide
radical action is needed

861
00:48:32,500 --> 00:48:35,740
and call another mum to the stand.

862
00:48:39,620 --> 00:48:42,180
Another day
in this Santa Maria courtroom,

863
00:48:42,380 --> 00:48:45,660
and another prosecution witness
in the trial of Michael Jackson.

864
00:48:45,860 --> 00:48:46,900
However, today's witness

865
00:48:47,100 --> 00:48:49,900
is a surprising choice
for the prosecution.

866
00:48:50,100 --> 00:48:54,180
With the prosecution
feeling their case is slipping away,

867
00:48:54,380 --> 00:48:58,460
they decide to take a huge gamble
on their next witness...

868
00:48:58,660 --> 00:49:01,740
Deborah, D-E-B-O-R-A-H

869
00:49:01,940 --> 00:49:03,380
Rowe, R-O-W-E.

870
00:49:03,580 --> 00:49:08,060
..someone closer to the defendant
than any other witness...

871
00:49:08,260 --> 00:49:12,700
Jackson, J-A-C-K-S-O-N.

872
00:49:12,900 --> 00:49:15,580
..the former wife
of Michael Jackson

873
00:49:15,780 --> 00:49:17,220
and the mother of his children.

874
00:49:19,580 --> 00:49:24,220
Rowe gave birth to two of Jackson's
children, Prince and Paris,

875
00:49:24,420 --> 00:49:28,020
in the late '90s,
but they separated in 1999.

876
00:49:28,220 --> 00:49:30,580
I remember having a conversation
with Steve Robel,

877
00:49:30,780 --> 00:49:33,380
the lead detective,
before Debbie testified,

878
00:49:33,580 --> 00:49:37,180
and they thought, you know,
this is huge for the prosecution.

879
00:49:37,380 --> 00:49:39,340
Michael Jackson's ex-wife
is gonna testify.

880
00:49:39,540 --> 00:49:43,780
But why would Rowe testify
against the father of her children?

881
00:49:46,860 --> 00:49:48,880
Do you know the defendant,
Michael Jackson,

882
00:49:49,080 --> 00:49:51,100
seated to my right,
with the long dark hair?

883
00:49:51,300 --> 00:49:52,500
Yes, I do.

884
00:49:53,540 --> 00:49:55,260
How do you know Mr Jackson?

885
00:49:55,460 --> 00:49:59,660
We've been friends,
and we were married.

886
00:49:59,860 --> 00:50:03,300
The prosecution understand
that Rowe is estranged from Jackson

887
00:50:03,500 --> 00:50:06,340
and hasn't seen her children
for nearly three years.

888
00:50:06,540 --> 00:50:08,620
I think they were expecting her

889
00:50:08,820 --> 00:50:12,220
to come up there and say that
she had concerns with his behaviour,

890
00:50:12,420 --> 00:50:16,260
that she even... she even warned him
about his behaviour.

891
00:50:16,460 --> 00:50:18,100
This is a key moment
for the prosecution.

892
00:50:18,300 --> 00:50:21,300
We were thinking that
this person is going to talk

893
00:50:21,500 --> 00:50:24,820
about some of the maybe shady things
that happened behind the scenes.

894
00:50:25,020 --> 00:50:26,980
Well, I think
the defence clearly anticipated

895
00:50:27,180 --> 00:50:29,740
that Debbie Rowe would say
very bad things about him.

896
00:50:29,940 --> 00:50:30,660
That was...

897
00:50:30,860 --> 00:50:34,820
All the evidence suggests that
that's what they anticipated.

898
00:50:35,020 --> 00:50:36,220
Like the Arvizo family,

899
00:50:36,420 --> 00:50:38,820
Rowe was also filmed
praising Jackson

900
00:50:39,020 --> 00:50:41,420
in response
to the Bashir documentary.

901
00:50:41,620 --> 00:50:43,180
And like the Arvizos,

902
00:50:43,380 --> 00:50:47,020
the prosecution believed
Jackson's ex-wife was coerced.

903
00:50:47,220 --> 00:50:50,460
And they expect her
to admit this on the stand.

904
00:50:52,820 --> 00:50:56,700
In that interview, what kind of
person did you say Michael was?

905
00:51:02,540 --> 00:51:06,780
Generous to a fault,
giving and kind.

906
00:51:09,220 --> 00:51:11,500
When she actually gave evidence,
she did the reverse

907
00:51:11,700 --> 00:51:13,140
and supported the defence case.

908
00:51:13,340 --> 00:51:14,900
She really did this 180.

909
00:51:15,100 --> 00:51:18,780
She says Michael Jackson
is "great with kids,

910
00:51:18,980 --> 00:51:20,940
"puts other people ahead of him".

911
00:51:21,140 --> 00:51:24,780
So, you know, that is only good
for the defence at this point.

912
00:51:27,060 --> 00:51:28,940
The prosecutors are shocked.

913
00:51:31,580 --> 00:51:34,140
Their gamble has backfired.

914
00:51:36,260 --> 00:51:38,620
What is it you're intending
to represent in this interview?

915
00:51:41,100 --> 00:51:44,380
Michael as a wonderful person

916
00:51:44,580 --> 00:51:49,220
and as a great father,
and generous and caring.

917
00:51:52,860 --> 00:51:57,180
I think the decision
to call her was a mistake.

918
00:51:57,380 --> 00:51:58,340
And suddenly, you're presented

919
00:51:58,540 --> 00:52:02,020
with a witness you didn't think
was gonna be helpful who is,

920
00:52:02,220 --> 00:52:04,180
then it's like anything in life,
you know.

921
00:52:04,380 --> 00:52:06,580
You've been given a free gift.
You're delighted about it.

922
00:52:07,540 --> 00:52:12,040
It showed or gave the impression
the prosecution was desperate.

923
00:52:12,240 --> 00:52:16,740
I don't know her personally,
but I knew she would never do...

924
00:52:16,940 --> 00:52:19,100
It's crazy to think
she would turn on Michael Jackson.

925
00:52:21,700 --> 00:52:25,200
Debbie Rowe has been
a disappointment to the prosecution.

926
00:52:25,400 --> 00:52:28,900
And four days later, after
nine weeks and over 80 witnesses,

927
00:52:29,100 --> 00:52:32,020
Sneddon and Zonen
finally rest their case.

928
00:52:33,420 --> 00:52:37,060
Now it's time for the defence to
present its arguments to the jury.

929
00:52:38,580 --> 00:52:41,060
And there is one question
on everyone's mind.

930
00:52:42,580 --> 00:52:46,320
I would say that
during this phase of the trial,

931
00:52:46,520 --> 00:52:50,090
almost every conversation
that we had on television

932
00:52:50,290 --> 00:52:53,860
and on radio and in the parking lot
and in restaurants

933
00:52:54,060 --> 00:52:55,660
was "Will Michael Jackson
take the stand?

934
00:52:55,860 --> 00:52:58,380
"Will he be called to testify
in his own defence?"

935
00:52:59,900 --> 00:53:03,240
Mesereau has to weigh up
the pros and cons

936
00:53:03,440 --> 00:53:06,010
of putting this global superstar
on the stand.

937
00:53:06,210 --> 00:53:08,580
He had a right
to take the stand.

938
00:53:08,780 --> 00:53:11,040
By law, you can,
if you're accused of something,

939
00:53:11,240 --> 00:53:13,500
you can get on the stand
and be your own witness.

940
00:53:13,700 --> 00:53:15,140
Uh, but he chose not to do that.

941
00:53:16,380 --> 00:53:18,140
Can you imagine
the cross-examination

942
00:53:18,340 --> 00:53:20,980
that Tom Sneddon would have with
Michael Jackson on the stand

943
00:53:21,180 --> 00:53:22,100
after all this time?

944
00:53:22,300 --> 00:53:25,660
This is a prosecutor who has
been trying to get Michael Jackson

945
00:53:25,860 --> 00:53:28,540
in a courtroom and on
a witness stand for years and years.

946
00:53:28,740 --> 00:53:30,700
And now here's the moment

947
00:53:30,900 --> 00:53:33,940
that would have opened up,
really, just a huge can of worms.

948
00:53:34,140 --> 00:53:37,460
He was very meek,
very mild, very quiet.

949
00:53:37,660 --> 00:53:42,300
And the notion that he would
have forcefully defended himself

950
00:53:42,500 --> 00:53:45,420
against these allegations
seems a little far-fetched.

951
00:53:50,020 --> 00:53:52,420
Instead of calling Mr Jackson,

952
00:53:52,620 --> 00:53:56,340
the defence begins its case
by calling forward witnesses

953
00:53:56,540 --> 00:53:59,620
who'd known the singer
when they were young boys.

954
00:53:59,820 --> 00:54:02,900
Good afternoon, Mr Robson.
Hey, how are you doing?

955
00:54:03,100 --> 00:54:05,860
How old are you?
I'm 22.

956
00:54:06,060 --> 00:54:07,500
Wade Robson was called
by the defence

957
00:54:07,700 --> 00:54:10,300
to say that he'd befriended
Michael Jackson,

958
00:54:10,500 --> 00:54:12,420
that he'd, as a child,
he'd often go to Neverland,

959
00:54:12,620 --> 00:54:14,020
he'd sleep over there.

960
00:54:14,220 --> 00:54:19,180
Mr Robson, did Michael Jackson
ever molest you at any time?

961
00:54:19,380 --> 00:54:21,340
Absolutely not.

962
00:54:21,540 --> 00:54:25,740
The defence clearly decided
to call witnesses

963
00:54:25,940 --> 00:54:30,980
who had not been the subject
to any sort of molestation at all.

964
00:54:31,180 --> 00:54:36,220
Mr Robson, did Michael Jackson
ever touch you in a sexual way?

965
00:54:36,420 --> 00:54:38,060
Never, no.

966
00:54:38,260 --> 00:54:41,860
This was powerful evidence
in the case.

967
00:54:42,060 --> 00:54:47,020
Mr Robson, has Michael Jackson ever
inappropriately touched

968
00:54:47,220 --> 00:54:50,860
any part of your body at any time?

969
00:54:51,060 --> 00:54:52,580
No.

970
00:54:56,060 --> 00:54:57,340
In cross-examination,

971
00:54:57,540 --> 00:55:01,720
the prosecution tried to sow doubt
in the jury's mind

972
00:55:01,920 --> 00:55:06,100
by undermining what is potentially
very strong testimony.

973
00:55:06,300 --> 00:55:09,700
You're saying nothing happened,
is that right?

974
00:55:09,900 --> 00:55:10,780
Yes.

975
00:55:11,980 --> 00:55:15,780
What you're really saying is nothing
happened while you were awake.

976
00:55:15,980 --> 00:55:17,540
Isn't that true?

977
00:55:17,740 --> 00:55:20,380
I'm telling you
that nothing ever happened.

978
00:55:22,140 --> 00:55:25,500
Mr Robson, when you were asleep,

979
00:55:25,700 --> 00:55:28,620
you wouldn't have known what had
happened, particularly at age seven.

980
00:55:28,820 --> 00:55:29,700
Would you have?

981
00:55:31,100 --> 00:55:33,780
I would think something like that
would wake me up.

982
00:55:35,340 --> 00:55:37,640
What is a witness supposed to say
when he's asked,

983
00:55:37,840 --> 00:55:39,940
"Is it possible you were abused
when you were asleep?"

984
00:55:40,140 --> 00:55:42,860
And what can a witness say,
other than that "I was asleep"?

985
00:55:43,060 --> 00:55:46,660
This seems to me
to be highly improbable

986
00:55:46,860 --> 00:55:49,820
and must have seemed
highly improbable to the jury.

987
00:55:50,020 --> 00:55:52,980
And the fact that
the prosecution were suggesting it

988
00:55:53,180 --> 00:55:55,380
does rather smack of desperation.

989
00:55:55,580 --> 00:55:57,780
It's all... It's a bit farcical.

990
00:56:01,340 --> 00:56:04,300
The next defence witness
is Macaulay Culkin,

991
00:56:04,500 --> 00:56:06,500
the star of Home Alone

992
00:56:06,700 --> 00:56:11,100
and a long-time friend of Jackson
as a young boy and as a teenager.

993
00:56:11,300 --> 00:56:14,780
There was a fair amount of
anticipation with the Culkin case

994
00:56:14,980 --> 00:56:16,300
because he was well known,

995
00:56:16,500 --> 00:56:19,620
and I think people were very
interested in what he had to say.

996
00:56:21,980 --> 00:56:26,780
There had been rumours that he had
been molested by Michael Jackson,

997
00:56:26,980 --> 00:56:29,460
and then, when Macaulay Culkin
got on the stand,

998
00:56:29,660 --> 00:56:32,220
he saw Michael, and he just melted.

999
00:56:32,420 --> 00:56:34,380
Just like Wade Robson,

1000
00:56:34,580 --> 00:56:37,180
Macaulay Culkin spent
long periods of time

1001
00:56:37,380 --> 00:56:40,620
hanging out with Michael Jackson
at Neverland.

1002
00:56:40,820 --> 00:56:44,060
He was adamant
that he had never been molested.

1003
00:56:44,260 --> 00:56:46,580
The strategy
with these two witnesses

1004
00:56:46,780 --> 00:56:48,460
was to corroborate the notion

1005
00:56:48,660 --> 00:56:51,020
that Michael had never engaged
in sexual abuse.

1006
00:56:51,220 --> 00:56:53,220
That's good for the defence.

1007
00:56:55,220 --> 00:56:59,420
Over 14 days,
the defence calls 50 witnesses,

1008
00:56:59,620 --> 00:57:03,700
and this includes other celebrities
there to defend Jackson's good name.

1009
00:57:03,900 --> 00:57:07,980
For the defence, we practically had
this conga line of celebrities -

1010
00:57:08,180 --> 00:57:12,260
Chris Tucker, George Lopez,
Jay Leno.

1011
00:57:13,500 --> 00:57:16,340
If a celebrity tells
you something, it must be the truth.

1012
00:57:16,540 --> 00:57:20,340
They pay more attention and
they put more weight on celebrity.

1013
00:57:20,540 --> 00:57:21,980
We hold them up as royalty.

1014
00:57:22,180 --> 00:57:24,860
And so Macaulay Culkin
was seen as royalty.

1015
00:57:25,060 --> 00:57:28,140
He's a celebrity.
He's a... You know, he's an icon.

1016
00:57:28,340 --> 00:57:30,340
He's a god to some of them.

1017
00:57:30,540 --> 00:57:32,460
The prosecution found it difficult

1018
00:57:32,660 --> 00:57:34,460
to undermine the testimony
of these stars.

1019
00:57:35,780 --> 00:57:38,980
I think the prosecution
didn't see it coming,

1020
00:57:39,180 --> 00:57:42,380
and it seemed like
they were very unprepared.

1021
00:57:48,540 --> 00:57:50,340
With the defence resting its case,

1022
00:57:50,540 --> 00:57:52,860
the judge is ready
to send the jury out.

1023
00:57:53,060 --> 00:57:57,980
But the prosecution asks if it can
present one final piece of evidence.

1024
00:57:59,260 --> 00:58:03,180
It's a video of Gavin giving
a police interview,

1025
00:58:03,380 --> 00:58:06,700
shortly after he claimed
he was abused.

1026
00:58:06,900 --> 00:58:07,780
I think that every time

1027
00:58:07,980 --> 00:58:11,420
that we have seen a police interview
played in a court of law,

1028
00:58:11,620 --> 00:58:14,540
it's very impactful
because it's in the moment.

1029
00:58:14,740 --> 00:58:16,340
Sneddon wasn't allowed
to show it before

1030
00:58:16,540 --> 00:58:20,740
because Gavin had testified
in court in person instead.

1031
00:58:20,940 --> 00:58:25,700
The prosecution chose to show
that tape at the end of the trial

1032
00:58:25,900 --> 00:58:29,220
because it was a way
of reminding the jury

1033
00:58:29,420 --> 00:58:31,500
of the central element of the case.

1034
00:58:33,060 --> 00:58:35,900
"This man molested me."

1035
00:58:36,100 --> 00:58:38,380
And that's it.
That's the heart of it.

1036
00:58:38,580 --> 00:58:40,780
Did he do it, or didn't he?

1037
00:58:40,980 --> 00:58:44,460
The prosecution convinced the judge
to change his mind,

1038
00:58:44,660 --> 00:58:47,180
concerned the defence
have made Gavin look

1039
00:58:47,380 --> 00:58:48,900
like he is making things up.

1040
00:58:49,100 --> 00:58:51,820
Sneddon wants jurors
to see how he came across

1041
00:58:52,020 --> 00:58:53,580
when he first gave evidence.

1042
00:59:05,260 --> 00:59:06,980
The video was so powerful,

1043
00:59:07,180 --> 00:59:11,660
cos you saw this child
squirming in his seat,

1044
00:59:11,860 --> 00:59:13,420
and you could see clearly

1045
00:59:13,620 --> 00:59:16,760
that he wasn't uncomfortable
because of the questions -

1046
00:59:16,960 --> 00:59:20,100
he was uncomfortable because
something happened to him.

1047
00:59:32,060 --> 00:59:33,020
Yeah.

1048
00:59:33,220 --> 00:59:38,380
The true, unvarnished truth is
what prosecutors say he is giving,

1049
00:59:38,580 --> 00:59:40,220
the truth
of what happened to him.

1050
00:59:40,420 --> 00:59:42,500
For a witness like Gavin,

1051
00:59:42,700 --> 00:59:45,180
who's been heavily criticised
during the trial

1052
00:59:45,380 --> 00:59:46,380
and made to look like a liar,

1053
00:59:46,580 --> 00:59:49,180
then to be portrayed
on the original police video

1054
00:59:49,380 --> 00:59:52,060
as being vulnerable and distressed

1055
00:59:52,260 --> 00:59:55,380
and... and very different
to how he's been portrayed,

1056
00:59:55,580 --> 00:59:57,980
could be extremely powerful
for the prosecution.

1057
00:59:58,180 --> 01:00:03,420
I think the demeanour of a child
when giving an account of abuse

1058
01:00:03,620 --> 01:00:07,820
can be very powerful evidence
in front of a jury.

1059
01:00:08,020 --> 01:00:10,940
I thought that
that was brilliant

1060
01:00:11,140 --> 01:00:14,060
to... to leave the jury with that.

1061
01:00:14,260 --> 01:00:16,420
And because of that,

1062
01:00:16,620 --> 01:00:20,340
I thought that they had
a good chance of a conviction.

1063
01:00:20,540 --> 01:00:27,100
It is time for the jury to decide
if Michael Jackson is guilty or not.

1064
01:00:29,940 --> 01:00:32,460
The jury in the four-month
trial of Michael Jackson

1065
01:00:32,660 --> 01:00:33,740
for molestation of a child

1066
01:00:33,940 --> 01:00:36,860
is expected to begin
their deliberations today.

1067
01:00:37,060 --> 01:00:40,740
The law says that there has
to be no doubt in a juror's mind.

1068
01:00:40,940 --> 01:00:43,940
If you're voting a certain way
in a case like this,

1069
01:00:44,140 --> 01:00:46,440
it's got to be ironclad.

1070
01:00:46,640 --> 01:00:48,740
After four months in court,

1071
01:00:48,940 --> 01:00:51,300
the judge instructs the jury
to retire

1072
01:00:51,500 --> 01:00:52,780
and consider their verdicts.

1073
01:00:54,900 --> 01:00:56,260
There was really no way of telling,

1074
01:00:56,460 --> 01:00:58,860
because a lot
of the prosecution's testimony

1075
01:00:59,060 --> 01:01:02,300
had been undermined by the defence.

1076
01:01:02,500 --> 01:01:06,740
And so you didn't know
how it would... how it would land.

1077
01:01:07,900 --> 01:01:11,140
It's an anxious wait
for both legal teams.

1078
01:01:11,340 --> 01:01:15,320
I would have thought the defence
were feeling relatively optimistic.

1079
01:01:15,520 --> 01:01:19,500
I think there was a feeling that...
that he would be found guilty.

1080
01:01:19,700 --> 01:01:21,020
Is this gonna be a hung jury?

1081
01:01:21,220 --> 01:01:22,340
Is this gonna be a mistrial,

1082
01:01:22,540 --> 01:01:24,700
after everything
that everybody's been through?

1083
01:01:24,900 --> 01:01:27,660
There was a lot of question
about how this was gonna end.

1084
01:01:27,860 --> 01:01:30,340
I mean, it was a nail-biter.

1085
01:01:33,660 --> 01:01:37,900
One day passes, then a second,
and no word from the jury.

1086
01:01:40,260 --> 01:01:43,500
Every day we went to the courthouse,
we're like, "Today's the day."

1087
01:01:43,700 --> 01:01:45,260
And then it wasn't.
And then it wasn't.

1088
01:01:45,460 --> 01:01:48,500
It was a lot of tension,
and the longer they stay out...

1089
01:01:49,820 --> 01:01:52,540
..you're thinking,
"OK, what's going on here?"

1090
01:01:52,740 --> 01:01:55,860
It was really extraordinary.

1091
01:01:56,060 --> 01:01:58,920
I mean, we'd waited, what,
seven days?

1092
01:01:59,120 --> 01:02:01,980
Usually, at a murder trial,
you know,

1093
01:02:02,180 --> 01:02:03,020
people will take their time.

1094
01:02:03,220 --> 01:02:04,500
It's somebody's life on the line.

1095
01:02:04,700 --> 01:02:07,500
And this was Michael Jackson's life
that was on the line.

1096
01:02:10,660 --> 01:02:14,500
Eventually, after seven days
of deliberating the evidence,

1097
01:02:14,700 --> 01:02:15,860
the jury returns.

1098
01:02:17,380 --> 01:02:22,260
When that announcement was made that
the jury came up with a verdict,

1099
01:02:22,460 --> 01:02:24,500
it was like an explosion.

1100
01:02:24,700 --> 01:02:27,300
I mean, people came from everywhere.

1101
01:02:27,500 --> 01:02:30,940
We had fans, we had protesters,
the world's media.

1102
01:02:31,140 --> 01:02:33,220
Everybody swarmed this courthouse.

1103
01:02:38,380 --> 01:02:40,920
The people
of the state of California,

1104
01:02:41,120 --> 01:02:43,660
Plaintiff versus
Michael Joe Jackson,

1105
01:02:43,860 --> 01:02:49,220
defendant case number 1133603.

1106
01:02:49,420 --> 01:02:51,020
Count one, verdict.

1107
01:02:53,740 --> 01:02:56,940
The crowd was on edge.

1108
01:02:57,140 --> 01:02:59,900
Hundreds of them,
Michael Jackson fans,

1109
01:03:00,100 --> 01:03:04,860
who really had their...
their hearts in their mouths.

1110
01:03:05,060 --> 01:03:08,180
We, the jury
in the above entitled case

1111
01:03:08,380 --> 01:03:11,200
find the defendant
not guilty of conspiracy

1112
01:03:11,400 --> 01:03:14,410
as charged
in count one of the indictment.

1113
01:03:14,610 --> 01:03:17,620
When that "not guilty" verdict
came out,

1114
01:03:17,820 --> 01:03:19,900
you could hear people screaming.

1115
01:03:20,100 --> 01:03:20,780
CROWD SCREAMS

1116
01:03:20,980 --> 01:03:23,260
They start yelling.

1117
01:03:23,460 --> 01:03:24,580
Second one.

1118
01:03:24,780 --> 01:03:26,940
We, the jury
in the above entitled case

1119
01:03:27,140 --> 01:03:31,900
find the defendant not guilty
of a lewd act upon a minor child.

1120
01:03:32,100 --> 01:03:34,260
Not guilty,
and then the third was...

1121
01:03:34,460 --> 01:03:35,700
Not guilty.

1122
01:03:35,900 --> 01:03:37,260
With each of them,

1123
01:03:37,460 --> 01:03:40,300
one of those fans
was releasing white doves.

1124
01:03:40,500 --> 01:03:43,340
And they are yelling,
and they're screaming,

1125
01:03:43,540 --> 01:03:45,300
and they're "Michael, Michael!"

1126
01:03:45,500 --> 01:03:46,780
Not guilty.

1127
01:03:46,980 --> 01:03:49,260
Not guilty.
Not guilty.

1128
01:03:49,460 --> 01:03:50,460
Not guilty.

1129
01:03:50,660 --> 01:03:53,300
He did it. He won.

1130
01:03:55,100 --> 01:03:57,380
It was one
of the most dramatic moments

1131
01:03:57,580 --> 01:03:59,660
that we have seen
inside of a courtroom.

1132
01:03:59,860 --> 01:04:05,020
All ten exonerating
Michael Jackson comprehensively.

1133
01:04:07,020 --> 01:04:13,380
It was an absolutely extraordinary
moment in criminal history.

1134
01:04:13,580 --> 01:04:15,620
I was stunned in the moment,

1135
01:04:15,820 --> 01:04:18,100
because I didn't think
he was walking out of that court.

1136
01:04:18,300 --> 01:04:19,180
He's a free man.

1137
01:04:20,580 --> 01:04:24,340
I recall people saying
that he had wiped away a tear,

1138
01:04:24,540 --> 01:04:27,260
that he looked visibly relieved.

1139
01:04:30,180 --> 01:04:32,340
Did he do it, or didn't he?

1140
01:04:32,540 --> 01:04:35,580
The trial was a way
of finding out if that was true.

1141
01:04:35,780 --> 01:04:37,180
For the second time,

1142
01:04:37,380 --> 01:04:40,900
prosecutor Sneddon has failed
to convict Michael Jackson,

1143
01:04:41,100 --> 01:04:43,860
who is cleared of all ten charges.

1144
01:04:44,060 --> 01:04:45,540
The verdict is no surprise.

1145
01:04:46,740 --> 01:04:51,100
I think it was
a weak prosecution case,

1146
01:04:51,300 --> 01:04:55,660
and I would have expected
most juries

1147
01:04:55,860 --> 01:04:57,940
to come to the same conclusion.

1148
01:04:58,140 --> 01:05:00,820
The case wasn't quite strong enough
to convict.

1149
01:05:03,100 --> 01:05:05,260
And then you add to that

1150
01:05:05,460 --> 01:05:08,020
the sheer celebrity
of Michael Jackson.

1151
01:05:08,220 --> 01:05:11,200
And I think the jury might have
been hesitant

1152
01:05:11,400 --> 01:05:14,380
to convict someone so well-known
and so renowned

1153
01:05:14,580 --> 01:05:16,660
and so loved by a lot of people.

1154
01:05:16,860 --> 01:05:17,620
More than any other place,

1155
01:05:17,820 --> 01:05:21,140
more than any other place
in the United States,

1156
01:05:21,340 --> 01:05:26,580
California has a very hard time
convicting its celebrities.

1157
01:05:26,780 --> 01:05:29,540
And in Michael Jackson's case,
the biggest celebrity in the world

1158
01:05:29,740 --> 01:05:31,740
was never going to prison.

1159
01:05:35,660 --> 01:05:38,980
Michael Jackson died in 2009.

1160
01:05:40,700 --> 01:05:43,540
14 years after testifying
for the defence,

1161
01:05:43,740 --> 01:05:46,580
Wade Robson admitted lying
under oath.

1162
01:05:47,900 --> 01:05:51,300
He claims he too
was molested by Jackson.

1163
01:05:53,260 --> 01:05:57,900
One other alleged victim
has since also come forward.
